From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 01:16:37 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a8xx: Make the crash state capture opt-in

On the OnePlus Pad 4 (Kaanapali, A840) a GPU fault from a client
(Chromium's GPU process) ended in a synchronous external abort in
a8xx_gpu_state_get(): the recovery worker's crash state capture read the
snapshot's GMU CX register list (adreno_snapshot_registers_v2() ->
reg_read() -> gmu_read()), the CPU took the abort, and the GPU recovery
never ran; the system hung until the watchdog restarted it. Before the
A8xx devcoredump series there was no gpu_state_get for A8xx and the same
faults recovered.

Capture the crash state only with msm.a8xx_crashstate=1 (default off).
The check comes before any register access, and returns -EOPNOTSUPP so
both the recovery worker and the debugfs "gpu" file skip it cleanly.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a8xx_gpu_state.c | 19 ++++++++++++++++---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_device.c  |  5 +++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_gpu.h     |  1 +
 3 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a8xx_gpu_state.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a8xx_gpu_state.c
index e4eb2f335a89..22b0d0a4ee1e 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a8xx_gpu_state.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a8xx_gpu_state.c
@@ -1062,13 +1062,26 @@ struct msm_gpu_state *a8xx_gpu_state_get(struct msm_gpu *gpu)
 	struct adreno_gpu *adreno_gpu = to_adreno_gpu(gpu);
 	struct a6xx_gpu *a6xx_gpu = to_a6xx_gpu(adreno_gpu);
 	struct adreno_gpu_state *state;
-	// TODO need to get status from SMMU on some gen8..
-	bool stalled = !!(gpu_read(gpu, REG_A8XX_RBBM_MISC_STATUS) &
-			A8XX_RBBM_MISC_STATUS_SMMU_STALLED_ON_FAULT);
+	bool stalled;
+
+	/*
+	 * On Kaanapali (A840) the snapshot's GMU CX register list raised a
+	 * synchronous external abort when read from the recovery worker, and
+	 * the GPU recovery never ran. Capture only when asked for.
+	 */
+	if (!READ_ONCE(a8xx_crashstate)) {
+		dev_info_once(&gpu->pdev->dev,
+			      "GPU crash state capture off (msm.a8xx_crashstate=1 enables it)\n");
+		return ERR_PTR(-EOPNOTSUPP);
+	}
 
 	if (!b)
 		return NULL;
 
+	// TODO need to get status from SMMU on some gen8..
+	stalled = !!(gpu_read(gpu, REG_A8XX_RBBM_MISC_STATUS) &
+		     A8XX_RBBM_MISC_STATUS_SMMU_STALLED_ON_FAULT);
+
 	state = kzalloc_obj(*state);
 	if (!state)
 		return ERR_PTR(-ENOMEM);
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_device.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_device.c
index 4699f2a93a2c..ff1b65652204 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_device.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_device.c
@@ -28,6 +28,11 @@ bool disable_acd;
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(disable_acd, "Forcefully disable GPU ACD");
 module_param_unsafe(disable_acd, bool, 0400);
 
+bool a8xx_crashstate;
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(a8xx_crashstate,
+		 "A8xx: capture the GPU crash state (devcoredump) at a GPU fault / hang (0=off (default), 1=on)");
+module_param(a8xx_crashstate, bool, 0600);
+
 bool enable_clx;
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(enable_clx, "Enable the GPU current limiter (CLX) on GPUs with a CLX table (0=off (default), 1=on)");
 module_param(enable_clx, bool, 0400);
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_gpu.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_gpu.h
index 05beb80e4ed0..d3bcdf180d4c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_gpu.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_gpu.h
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@
 
 extern bool snapshot_debugbus;
 extern bool enable_clx;
+extern bool a8xx_crashstate;
 
 enum {
 	ADRENO_FW_PM4 = 0,
